Relay patch 0003: no private window blur call.

libghostty exports ghostty_set_window_background_blur, which calls
CGSSetWindowBackgroundBlurRadius and CGSDefaultConnectionForThread:
private window server functions. An export is linked into the app
whether or not anything calls it, so the Mac binary imported both, and
App Review's automated check turned the build away for it (2026-11-16:
"The app uses or references the following non-public or deprecated
APIs: _CGSSetWindowBackgroundBlurRadius").

Relay doesn't blur its window's background and never called the
function, so this removes it, with its declaration in ghostty.h.
Scripts/check-store-export.py refuses an App Store binary that imports
a CGS function.

diff --git a/include/ghostty.h b/include/ghostty.h
index 5358aff..050fd1e 100644
--- a/include/ghostty.h
+++ b/include/ghostty.h
@@ -1308,10 +1308,6 @@ GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_inspector_metal_render(ghostty_inspector_t, void*, void
 GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_inspector_metal_shutdown(ghostty_inspector_t);
 #endif
 
-// APIs I'd like to get rid of eventually but are still needed for now.
-// Don't use these unless you know what you're doing.
-GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_set_window_background_blur(ghostty_app_t, void*);
-
 // Benchmark API, if available.
 GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_benchmark_cli(const char*, const char*);
 
